$NetBSD$

Apply the same fix to the option-format paths.

patch-autoopts_tpl_cmd-doc.tlib brings in the upstream fix for
ds-format, but the two option-format paths in the same file build the
converter name the same unconditional way, so a definitions file that
says

	option-format = 'mdoc';

still sends the template looking for a "mdoc2mdoc" converter that is
generated but not installed.  Upstream has not fixed these; this is
their ds-format fix applied to the remaining two places, written the
same way so it can be offered upstream as such.

Nothing in pkgsrc appears to use option-format = 'mdoc' today, so this
is a latent defect rather than an observed failure.

--- autoopts/tpl/cmd-doc.tlib.orig	2017-09-11 00:00:00.000000000 +0000
+++ autoopts/tpl/cmd-doc.tlib
@@ -151,7 +151,9 @@
         (define target-form   (if man-page "man" "mdoc"))
         (define source-form   (get "option-format" "texi"))
         (define converter     (string-append source-form "2" target-form ))
-        (set! tmp-str (find-file converter))
+        (if (= source-form target-form)
+            (set! tmp-str (shell "command -v cat"))
+            (set! tmp-str (find-file converter)) )
 
         (if (not (defined? 'tmp-str))
             (error (string-append "cannot locate " converter)))
@@ -586,7 +588,9 @@
 
 (if formatted-doc
     (shell (string-append
-    "fn='" (find-file cvt-cmd)
+    "fn='" (if (= (get "option-format") "mdoc")
+               (shell "command -v cat")
+               (find-file cvt-cmd))
     "'\ntest -f ${fn} || die '" cvt-cmd " not found'\n"
     "${fn} <<\\_EndOfMdoc_ || die ${fn} failed in $PWD\n"
     (out-pop #t)
